From 141b97e99a63ecd888cf5d6cea2d96153e50f68b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:36:42 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] arm: add Axera AX620E (AX630C) SoC support

The AX620E family (AX630C) is a dual Cortex-A53 SoC used in the Sipeed
NanoKVM-Pro. U-Boot runs as BL33: the boot ROM loads a signed first-stage
loader which trains DRAM, locks the PLLs, sets every clock mux and muxes the
console and eMMC pads, then TF-A's BL31 enters U-Boot at EL1h. There is no
SPL and no low-level init here, so the whole SoC layer is a memory map and
the two DRAM hooks that read the device tree.

Signed-off-by: open-nanokvm-pro contributors <nanokvm@localhost>
---
 arch/arm/Kconfig             | 16 ++++++++
 arch/arm/Makefile            |  1 +
 arch/arm/mach-axera/Kconfig  | 27 ++++++++++++++
 arch/arm/mach-axera/Makefile |  5 +++
 arch/arm/mach-axera/soc.c    | 63 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/configs/ax630c.h     | 100 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 212 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/mach-axera/Kconfig
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/mach-axera/Makefile
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/mach-axera/soc.c
 create mode 100644 include/configs/ax630c.h

